   "failure_scenario": "An operator installs the source release with isolated production dependencies on a clean machine. The missing dependency prevents every CLI command, including daemon startup, from running.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: The offline frozen production install with --linker=isolated succeeded and exposed no root-level reflect-metadata package, but CLI execution succeeded because an unrelated ancestor node_modules supplied it. A resolution probe confirmed that external path, so this environment masks the clean-install startup failure.",
   "evidence": "HEAD adds the unconditional entry-point import `import \"reflect-metadata\";`. package.json does not declare it; bun.lock lists it only transitively under @simplewebauthn/server. The isolated-install probe printed `reflect-metadata exposed in installed root: false` and `transitive copy installed: true`. Base has the same dependency declarations but lacks the entry-point import, so it does not require this transitive package to resolve from application code."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Someone installs production dependencies with Bun's isolated linker instead of the default hoisted layout. The CLI entry point then imports a package that the project never declared, and every limitless command fails at startup with 'Cannot find package reflect-metadata'. The deploy, CI and gate setup all run a plain `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, which hoists the package to the top level, so it works today.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: an offline isolated install couldn't complete because the local Bun cache doesn't have every package (`failed to download @modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.30.1: ConnectionRefused` against a dead registry), and network is not allowed. With the default hoisted install, node_modules/reflect-metadata exists at the top level and `bun -e 'import \"reflect-metadata\"'` works.",
   "evidence": "HEAD src/cli/main.ts:2-3 adds `// WebAuthn's bundled dependencies need the polyfill...` and `import \"reflect-metadata\";`. Neither package.json nor bun.lock lists reflect-metadata among the root workspace's dependencies. The lockfile only has it as a dependency of `@simplewebauthn/server@14.0.3` (`\"reflect-metadata\": \"^0.2.2\"`), so it resolves only because the hoisted linker puts it at the top level. That makes it an undeclared (phantom) dependency added by this change. Every install path in the repo (ci.yml, packaged-smoke.yml, .limitless.toml setup, the OPERATIONS deploy) uses the default linker, which is why the impact is minor."
  }
